  "lessonRead3": "WEEK 4 Festival of Colors\nRead 3 of 3: Act Out the Story\nObjectives I am learning to:\n● communicate with my classmates about a story. (SEL7)\n● demonstrate eagerness and curiosity. (APL2)\n● act out characters and events from the story. (RL.PK.3)\nOpening Seat children around the perimeter of the rug.\nWe will read Festival of Colors again.\nLet’s get started.\nWhile reading Select several scenes (beginning, middle, end) to act out.\nAfter Reading Have a discussion about the experience.\nWhat did you think about acting out the story today?\nClosing We will act out other stories soon!\nStandards SEL7: The child will demonstrate the ability to communicate with others in\na variety of ways.\nAPL2: The child will demonstrate eagerness and curiosity as a learner.\nRL.PK.3. With prompting and support, act out characters and events from a\nstory or poem read aloud.\nOngoing\nassessment\nConsider how acting out the story worked, and listen to the children’s\nreflection afterward.\nNotes\nRead Aloud U2 W4\nFocus on Pre-K 3s | Boston Public Schools Early Childhood Department P-2\n",
